import Mathlib

/-! # B6-5 stage 5e: exact Taylor data of the 5d family along the 5c path

Literal rational data, through order seven in `θ`, of the Schlesinger residues, of the two
inverse-block frames and of the analytic numerator array of the 5d family along the 5c path
(G32 v0.16, §5.5(1)–(7), Lemma 5.8). These declarations are data, not a mathematical claim; the
claims are the statements of `NumeratorJet.lean`.

Computation. Exact rational arithmetic (Python, `gmpy2`), following the definitions of
`KernelFramesFamilyDefs.lean` and `SchlesingerPathDefs.lean` term by term. A moving residue is
written `A_x(θ) = Σ_c F_c(θ) x^c` in the basis `1, x, …, x⁵` of `ℚ[x]/(P_e)`, `e ∈ {5, −7}`, and
sums over the six roots of a fibre are traces of the quotient algebra (sums over pairs of roots
of different fibres are traces of `ℚ[x]/(P₅) ⊗ ℚ[y]/(P₋₇)`, where `x − y` is invertible); this is
the rationality of G32 v0.16, §5.5(1). The Taylor coefficients of the residues come from the
Schlesinger equations (`b65p_schlesingerField` along `b65p_poles`) and the initial residues
`b65p_initialResidue`; the eigenbases, gauges, inverse series, left eigenvectors, both systems,
both frames and the numerator array follow the 5d definitions as power series modulo `θ⁸`.
Consistency checks of the same run: the residue sum vanishes at every order; at `θ = 0` both
systems equal `b65k_rSystem` and `b65k_qSystem` entry by entry; the twelve unselected rows of
each system vanish on the frames at every order (also through order twelve); the products
`qᵀr` have no terms in `s⁰, …, s⁻³` at `∞`. The numerator array was compared with the export
`data/certificates/g32-rank/M_jets.json` only after it was computed.

HC no distance; AV milestone no distance.
-/

